<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Assassination Rogue in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>Assassination’s T16 set bonuses heading into Phase 5 are decent! The 2-piece provides us with energy reduction on Dispatch when we build a combo point with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=14190/seal-fate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_stayofexecution.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal Fate</span></a>, which is always appreciated. The 4-piece grants us Mastery that ramps up during <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=79140/vendetta">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_deadliness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vendetta</span></a> for each ability we cast against the target. Compared to Combat and Subtlety, I’d argue Assassination benefits most from its set bonuses.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
