<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as racial weapon expertise will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Dungeon or Raid bosses. Our Poisons are now also based off the melee hit table, meaning that 7.5% is all that it takes to ensure that our Poisons never miss. Your regular swings (white damage) still have a chance to miss up until the dual wield Hit cap of 26.5%. This is calculated by taking the base miss chance of 3%, adding the dual wield penalty of 19%, and then adding 1.5% per level above you that the enemy is for a total cap of 26.5%.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them when attacking from their front. For the vast majority of bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry from behind.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c4" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> <span class="c4">Gemming for Assassination Rogues</span></span></h2>Gemming is fairly straightforward throughout Mists of Pandaria. You look to get as much Agility as possible and tend to make socket bonus choices based if they will give you more Agility or equal Agility with additional secondary stats. The new <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> arrives in Phase 4. It'll require you to kill bosses in Throne of Thunder and acquire 20 <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94593/secrets-of-the-empire">
<img alt="Secrets of the Empire" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/secrets_of_the_empire_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Secrets of the Empire</span></a>, as well as 40 <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=72095/trillium-bar">
<img alt="Trillium Bar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ingot_trillium.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trillium Bar</span></a>. This new gem brings the buff <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=137596/capacitance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_purge.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitance</span></a>. The PPM for different specializations varies quite a bit.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76692/delicate-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
